// T2 - the class-diagram side, which the modeler itself never reaches.
//
// This is the legacy gap kept as-is during the FML migration: UMLEditor only creates the root
// model, and NO behaviour of this modeler ever calls UMLClassDiagram::init - so the diagram, its
// palette and its drop scheme have never been reachable from the model. A script can call it, and
// that is what this test does: it proves the diagram half is sound even though nothing wires it.

editorVM = load -r ["http://openflexo.org/uml-modeler/FML/UMLEditor.fml"];
modelVM = load -r ["http://openflexo.org/uml-modeler/FML/UMLEditor.fml/UMLModel.fml"];
diagramVM = load -r ["http://openflexo.org/uml-modeler/FML/UMLEditor.fml/UMLClassDiagram.fml"];
assert diagramVM != null;

service ResourceCenterService add_temp_rc;
editor = new UMLEditor::init() with (name="UMLEditorInstance");
model = editor.rootModel;

classDiagram = new UMLClassDiagram::init(model) with (name="ClassDiagram");
assert classDiagram != null;

// The TypedDiagram model slot resolved, on a diagram created in the temporary resource center.
assert classDiagram.diagram != null;
// init() hardcodes resourceName="diagram", so every instance yields a diagram of that name.
assert classDiagram.diagram.name == "diagram.diagram";

// The FMLRT slot points back at the model it was handed.
assert classDiagram.umlModel == model;

// A freshly created diagram is empty: init() draws nothing, it only creates the diagram resource.
assert classDiagram.diagram.shapes.size == 0;
assert classDiagram.flexoConceptInstances.size == 0;

// --- Why the drop scheme is NOT exercised here, pinned as measured -----------------------------
// `classDiagram.new ClassGR::dropClassGRAtTopLevel()` does return a ClassGR, but a DropScheme reads
// `topLevel`, a variable only a real drop supplies. Called from a script it half-executes: the
// first AddShape lands one orphan shape in the diagram, the five `container=main` ones do nothing,
// and every shape role - main, icon, header, properties, operations, headerOutline - stays null.
// Asserting on that would pin the behaviour of a mis-used API, not the modeler. The drop scheme
// needs a UI-level test (or a drop-context fixture) to be exercised faithfully.

log "Test PASSED: T2 - UMLClassDiagram is instantiable and creates its diagram, though nothing calls it";
